    "short_description": "Create a source connector, a destination connector, and the pipeline that connects them, end to end.",
    "body": "<h1>Building your first pipeline</h1>

{{ds:component/docs-toc|items_html=<li><a href="#create-a-source-connector">Create a source connector</a></li><li><a href="#create-a-destination-connector">Create a destination connector</a></li><li><a href="#create-the-pipeline">Create the pipeline</a></li><li><a href="#next-steps">Next steps</a></li>}}

<p>This guide walks through creating a <a href="{{cms:item/5ac66235-69dc-4092-b430-9d68837e0c76}}">pipeline</a> end to end: a source connector, a destination connector, and the pipeline that ties them together.</p>

{{ds:component/alert|variant=info|title=Before you start|body_html=<p>You'll need an API key. See <a href="{{cms:item/67e28ef9-df46-446a-9839-8f4bd0b23de1}}">Authentication</a> in Getting Started if you don't have one yet.</p>}}

<h2 id="create-a-source-connector">1. Create a source connector</h2>
<p>We'll pull orders from Postgres. See <a href="{{cms:item/7418c3d6-9ea1-4d1c-8d8f-73136f6b6abb}}">Connectors</a> for the full catalog of types.</p>

<h3>Using curl</h3>
{{ds:component/code-block|filename=create-source.sh|language=bash|code=curl -X POST https://api.godzilladocs.dev/v2/connectors \\\\\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $GODZILLA_API_KEY" \\\\\\n  -d '&#123;"type":"postgres","direction":"source","config":&#123;"connection_string":"postgres://..."&#125;&#125;'}}

<h3>Using Go</h3>
{{ds:component/code-block|filename=main.go|language=go|code=package main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\t"context"\\n\\t"fmt"\\n\\t"os"\\n\\n\\t"github.com/godzilla-sh/godzilla-go"\\n)\\n\\nfunc main() &#123;\\n\\tclient := godzilla.NewClient(\\n\\t\\tos.Getenv("GODZILLA_API_KEY"),\\n\\t)\\n\\n\\tconnector, err := client.Connectors.Create(context.Background(), &godzilla.CreateConnectorRequest&#123;\\n\\t\\tType:      "postgres",\\n\\t\\tDirection: "source",\\n\\t\\tConfig: map[string]interface()&#123;\\n\\t\\t\\t"connection_string": "postgres://...",\\n\\t\\t&#125;,\\n\\t&#125;)\\n\\tif err != nil &#123;\\n\\t\\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, "Error: %v\\n", err)\\n\\t\\tos.Exit(1)\\n\\t&#125;\\n\\n\\tfmt.Printf("Created source connector: %s\\n", connector.ID)\\n&#125;}}

<h2 id="create-a-destination-connector">2. Create a destination connector</h2>
<p>We'll write to Snowflake.</p>

<h3>Using curl</h3>
{{ds:component/code-block|filename=create-destination.sh|language=bash|code=curl -X POST https://api.godzilladocs.dev/v2/connectors \\\\\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer $GODZILLA_API_KEY" \\\\\\n  -d '&#123;"type":"snowflake","direction":"destination","config":&#123;"account":"..."&#125;&#125;'}}

